  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Corruption Hunter Network 2026-2029</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Corruption Hunters network is a network against corruption with participants from between 15-20 countries  mostly law enforcement/prosecutors and head of anti-corruption agencies, and special invited persons. from academia, media and civil society. The network has met regularly since 2005 with a handful of the original members still participating, By mid 2025  the participants/guests come from: Zambia, Namibia, South Africa, Nigeriai, Argentina, Mauritsius,  Costa Rica, Sao Tome e Pricipe, Brazil, Seychelles, Italy, Switzerland, France, Norway, Sweden,  USA, Lebanon and the Mena region.  In addition participants from UNODC, U4 Anti-Corruption Resource centre and Basel Institute/International Centre for Asset Recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
